cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mbfit: multiband magnetotransport analysis"
message: "If you use this program in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Kwang-Tak
    alias: ktkim
    # Add your ORCID here if you have one -- it is what makes a citation
    # resolve to you rather than to a name many people share:
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KTKim1112/multiband-hall-drude"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-30"
abstract: >-
  Fits the longitudinal and Hall resistivity of a multicarrier conductor
  together with a classical multiband Drude model, and reports how far the
  measurement determines the answer before reporting the answer. The number of
  conduction channels is bounded above by a mobility spectrum and below by what
  the sweep requires; each candidate is judged by four gates and graded by the
  conditioning of the fit, because a curve can be followed closely while the
  densities and mobilities behind it are not determined at all.
keywords:
  - magnetotransport
  - Hall effect
  - carrier mobility
  - carrier concentration
  - multicarrier analysis
  - mobility spectrum
  - semiconductor characterisation
  - Drude model
